 ## Unreleased
 
+- Complete CAP-014’s native proxy-vote proof: parse CSV exports and bind each exercised customer, request, source and recorder to one row using the authenticated actor. Extend the existing inbox, request-page and Zendesk journeys without removing their duplicate, collapse, privacy or permission assertions, and cite the existing UserVoice historical-proxy journey. Mark CAP-014 done; live Zendesk installation remains field proof R-5. No runtime, migration or configuration change is required.
+
 - Complete NOTIFY-005’s existing route journeys: requester status history retains each event identity, body and publication time after retry exhaustion, ambiguous sends and interrupted attempts; operator review reminders retain the due decision, review date and notification identity through the same failures and later drains. Preserve bounded retries, durable operator failure visibility and unknown-send no-replay checks. No runtime, migration or configuration change is required; other clauses and field-proof holds remain unchanged.
 
 - Prove EVID-007 suggestion requests leave existing request and bet evidence links, evidence contributions, merge history, canonical targets, requests, evidence wording and pending submissions unchanged before any explicit action. Retain published-only, deterministic no-model matching and explicit vote and follow assertions, including case, punctuation and Unicode coverage. Rank indexed ASCII terms inside D1 while preserving the full Unicode matcher. Migration 0109 adds expression indexes and read-only views; apply it with the existing migration runner and retain those schema objects on source rollback. Existing product records stay unchanged. Add a manual built-Worker capacity journey for exact, partial, absent and Unicode queries at the declared request, board and requester limits, and close EVID-007’s native proof gap. Automatic model rules remain in their existing clauses.
